mation\n\nGodot v4.5.beta1.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1060 6GB (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-3570K CPU @ 3.40GHz (4 threads) - 15.95 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI have constant colors `c1`, `c2` and a non-constant color `c3`:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17926ebf-05ad-4ca5-8bef-2a182d415e86)\n\n`c2` and `c3` are shown to have the same color, green. But `c3` is a non-constant color, it is not green. In this exact case the `c3`'s color would be yellow, but for example in the following code the actual color would change in every while loop.\n\n```gdscript\nvar red := 0.0\nwhile red < 1.0:\n\tvar color = Color(red, 1, 0)\n\tred += 0.1\n\t...\n```\n\nIf I click the `c3`'s color rectangle I can choose a new color. That will overwrite the variable `red` and replace it with a constant number:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/245285b3-3935-4c20-9b78-6c9e6333d2ee)\n\nI would expect that non-constant colors would not display the color rectangle and they would not be editable at all with the inline color picker.\n\nIn the following case the color could be considered being quite constant, but I would still handle this as a non-constant color. Having the color picker being able to lock red component to value of RED and being able to change only green, blue and alpha components might be the \"correct\" way of handling this, but probably far too complicated for rare use cases.\n\n```gdscript\n\tconst RED := 1\n\tvar c4 = Color(RED, 1, 0)\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```gdscript\n\tvar red = 1\n\tvar c1 = Color(1, 1, 0)\n\tvar c2 = Color(0, 1, 0)\n\tvar c3 = Color(red, 1, 0)\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107725/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107725/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}